WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.195
Lesson 10.1.

00:00:02.195 --> 00:00:06.910
Fixed-rate yield: principal and yield tokens (PT/YT).

00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:09.462
By the end of this lesson, you'll be able

00:00:09.462 --> 00:00:12.561
to lock a fixed return using principal tokens, and

00:00:12.561 --> 00:00:15.295
price a yield token against its implied rate.

00:00:16.595 --> 00:00:17.885
Here's the plan.

00:00:17.885 --> 00:00:19.570
First, the key ideas.

00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:22.285
Then, a worked example, step by step.

00:00:22.285 --> 00:00:23.810
Then, your checklist.

00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:25.972
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:27.272 --> 00:00:31.658
Yield tokenization takes a yield-bearing asset (a staked

00:00:31.658 --> 00:00:35.814
asset, a lending receipt, a stablecoin savings token)

00:00:35.814 --> 00:00:39.046
and splits it into two tokens that mature

00:00:39.046 --> 00:00:41.347
on a set date: trades at a

00:00:41.347 --> 00:00:45.232
discount before then. Buy the discount, hold to

00:00:45.232 --> 00:00:48.952
maturity, and your return is fixed. the underlying

00:00:48.952 --> 00:00:53.112
earns until maturity, then is worth zero. PT +

00:00:53.112 --> 00:00:56.119
YT = one unit of the underlying.

00:00:56.119 --> 00:00:59.517
The PT price implies a fixed rate;

00:00:59.517 --> 00:01:02.607
the YT is a bet that realised yield

00:01:02.607 --> 00:01:05.182
beats it. fixed APY = (1 ÷ PT

00:01:05.182 --> 00:01:09.044
price)^(365 ÷ days) − 1 First, PT (principal

00:01:09.044 --> 00:01:13.722
token): redeems 1:1 for the underlying at maturity.

00:01:13.722 --> 00:01:14.457
It.

00:01:14.457 --> 00:01:17.545
And finally, YT (yield token): receives all

00:01:17.545 --> 00:01:20.212
the variable yield (and often points).

00:01:21.512 --> 00:01:24.010
Let's look at the chart: PT

00:01:24.010 --> 00:01:27.522
price converges to 1.00 at maturity.

00:01:27.522 --> 00:01:29.082
Take a moment with it.

00:01:29.082 --> 00:01:31.492
It's everything we've just said, in one picture.

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:35.307
Let's work an example, step by step.

00:01:35.307 --> 00:01:37.828
A stablecoin savings token has a P.T. maturing in

00:01:37.828 --> 00:01:40.350
180 days, priced at 0.96. yield (plus any points)

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:42.818
averages above about 8.6% for the 180 days.

00:01:42.818 --> 00:01:46.308
Near maturity, small discounts are big rates: P.T. at

00:01:46.308 --> 00:01:49.128
0.985 with 60 days left to 9.63% A.P.Y.

00:01:49.128 --> 00:01:58.066
Check liquidity before chasing these; exiting

00:01:58.066 --> 00:02:04.973
early means selling into the pool.

00:02:04.973 --> 00:02:11.847
$100,000 buys about 104,167 P.T. to redeems for

00:02:11.847 --> 00:02:18.448
about 104,167 of the underlying at maturity.

00:02:18.448 --> 00:02:22.223
The Y.T. costs about 0.04 per unit.

00:02:22.223 --> 00:02:25.258
It only profits if the underlying's realised.

00:02:25.258 --> 00:02:28.253
You can check every number with the program's calculator.

00:02:29.553 --> 00:02:32.792
PT: the underlying's credit/depeg risk, and

00:02:32.792 --> 00:02:35.153
liquidity if you exit early.

00:02:35.153 --> 00:02:38.548
YT: falling yields, and time (it decays to zero).

00:02:39.848 --> 00:02:41.308
Here's your checklist.

00:02:41.308 --> 00:02:42.843
Do it now, for real.

00:02:42.843 --> 00:02:45.758
First, I'd hold the underlying asset anyway.

00:02:45.758 --> 00:02:48.333
Next, Maturity date matches when I'll

00:02:48.333 --> 00:02:51.073
need the money (Module 12.4 ladder).

00:02:51.073 --> 00:02:53.878
Then, Pool depth checked for an early exit.

00:02:53.878 --> 00:02:57.868
And finally, YT sized as speculation, not income.

00:02:59.168 --> 00:03:00.378
Question 1.

00:03:00.378 --> 00:03:05.318
PT at 0.97, 120 days to maturity.

00:03:05.318 --> 00:03:06.603
Fixed APY?

00:03:11.023 --> 00:03:19.428
The answer: (1/0.97)^(365/120) − 1 ≈ 9.7%.

00:03:20.728 --> 00:03:21.973
Question 2.

00:03:21.973 --> 00:03:25.208
Does buying PT remove the underlying's risk?

00:03:29.628 --> 00:03:32.093
The answer: No. It fixes the rate.

00:03:32.093 --> 00:03:35.141
If the underlying depegs or is exploited,

00:03:35.141 --> 00:03:37.753
the PT redeems into a damaged asset.

00:03:39.053 --> 00:03:40.323
Question 3.

00:03:40.323 --> 00:03:43.078
What must happen for a YT to profit?

00:03:47.498 --> 00:03:51.073
The answer: Realised variable yield plus points must

00:03:51.073 --> 00:03:53.838
beat the implied rate priced into the PT.

00:03:55.138 --> 00:03:56.383
Let's recap.

00:03:56.383 --> 00:03:59.009
PT (principal token): redeems 1:1

00:03:59.009 --> 00:04:01.703
for the underlying at maturity.

00:04:01.703 --> 00:04:04.163
YT (yield token): receives all the

00:04:04.163 --> 00:04:06.552
variable yield (and often points).

00:04:07.852 --> 00:04:10.367
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:04:10.367 --> 00:04:14.157
Next up, Lesson 10.2: Cash-and-carry basis trades.
